- Point the AppHost at your Azure OpenAI resource and give it the resource's key, which stays out of the repository: `dotnet user-secrets set Parameters:azure-openai-endpoint https://<resource>.openai.azure.com --project src/AppHost` and `dotnet user-secrets set Parameters:azure-openai-api-key <key> --project src/AppHost`. The parameter `azure-openai-deployment` (`gpt-5-mini` by default) must name a deployment in that resource. Without them the host cannot call the model; the tests never need them.